@baseUrl = http://localhost:5279
@idempotencyKey = 665886cf-e957-4555-b4ca-ad7b6baab8e5
@correlationId = f1382b1c-4525-4fd5-87cc-90803693a898

### Seed sample voyage + bookings (replace ids below from the response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dev/seed
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "voyageCapacity": 2
}

### Confirm booking A
@bookingAId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingAId}}/confirm
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}
X-Correlation-ID: {{correlationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expectedVersion": null
}

### Scenario B — replay the same confirmation (idempotent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingAId}}/confirm
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}
X-Correlation-ID: {{correlationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Scenario C — same Idempotency-Key, different booking
@bookingBId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingBId}}/confirm
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}
X-Correlation-ID: {{correlationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Scenario A — confirm booking B with its own key (run in parallel with booking A)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingBId}}/confirm
Idempotency-Key: 7c1a2b3d-e4f5-4678-9abc-def012345678
X-Correlation-ID: {{correlationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Scenario D — voyage already closed for booking
@closedVoyageBookingId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{closedVoyageBookingId}}/confirm
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555
X-Correlation-ID: {{correlationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Get booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingAId}}

### Scenario E — process outbox (set Outbox:SimulatePublishFailure to leave Pending, then set false and process again)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dev/outbox/process

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
